<!-- PHASE 1 -->
<details class="sec phase" id="phase1" open>
<summary><h2 class="p1">Phase 1 <span class="tag">Weeks 1–3</span></h2></summary>
<p class="sub">Straight-on climbing only. Vertical to ~10° overhang. Big footholds, feet directly beneath hips, every foot placement static and deliberate. Operated leg tolerance — not grade — is the rate limiter.</p>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Block A · Lock-off Ladders</h3><div class="freq">15:00–30:00 · both sessions</div></div>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Drill</th><th>Sets × Reps</th><th>Rest</th><th>Target / RPE</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Mirrored lock-off ladder — pull to lock, hold, move up one hold. 6 moves per side.<span class="note">Left side, then identical sequence mirrored right.</span><span class="knee ok">Feet static, hip-width</span></td>
      <td class="num">4 × 6 moves<br>(2L / 2R)</td>
      <td class="num">2:30</td>
      <td>3-sec lock each move · RPE 6–7</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Gaston → undercling ladder — alternate gaston and undercling up the grid.<span class="knee ok">No high steps</span></td>
      <td class="num">3 × 6 moves<br>(mirrored)</td>
      <td class="num">2:00</td>
      <td>Smooth, zero foot readjustments · RPE 6</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Block B · Tension &amp; Control</h3><div class="freq">30:00–45:00 · both sessions</div></div>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Drill</th><th>Sets × Reps</th><th>Rest</th><th>Target / RPE</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>3-second pause traverse — pause 3s after every hand move, hips stay square to wall.</td>
      <td class="num">3 × 10 moves</td>
      <td class="num">2:00</td>
      <td>No momentum, silent feet · RPE 5–6</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Downclimb repeats — climb 6 moves up, downclimb the identical sequence.<span class="knee ok">Zero drops — this is the knee-protection drill</span></td>
      <td class="num">3 × 12 moves<br>(6 up / 6 down)</td>
      <td class="num">2:30</td>
      <td>Down as controlled as up · RPE 6</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

</details>

<!-- PHASE 2 -->
<details class="sec phase" id="phase2">
<summary><h2 class="p2">Phase 2 <span class="tag">Weeks 4–6</span></h2></summary>
<p class="sub">Gentle knee involvement begins. Add shallow backsteps and outside flags — the foot must pivot freely; never lock the foot and twist. Steps may rise to mid-thigh from Week 5. Angle to ~20° overhang if pain-free.</p>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Block A · Rotational Prep</h3><div class="freq">15:00–30:00 · both sessions</div></div>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Drill</th><th>Sets × Reps</th><th>Rest</th><th>Target / RPE</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Shallow backstep ladder — outside edge, hip turns in ≤45°, 6 moves per side.<span class="knee cau">Foot pivots freely on hold</span></td>
      <td class="num">4 × 6 moves<br>(2L / 2R)</td>
      <td class="num">2:30</td>
      <td>Compare op-leg vs. non-op tolerance · RPE 6</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Outside flag circuit — flag the free leg on every second move.<span class="knee cau">Straight flagging leg only</span></td>
      <td class="num">3 × 8 moves<br>(mirrored)</td>
      <td class="num">2:00</td>
      <td>Hip stays close to wall · RPE 6–7</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Block B · Loaded Control</h3><div class="freq">30:00–45:00 · both sessions</div></div>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Drill</th><th>Sets × Reps</th><th>Rest</th><th>Target / RPE</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Mid-thigh high-step repeats — deliberate high step, weight through the whole foot, stand up slowly (3s).<span class="knee cau">Wk 5+ only · alternate legs each rep</span></td>
      <td class="num">3 × 6 reps<br>(3 per leg)</td>
      <td class="num">2:30</td>
      <td>No knee wobble on stand-up · RPE 7</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>3-second pause ladder on smaller feet — Phase 1 pause drill, footholds one size down.</td>
      <td class="num">3 × 8 moves</td>
      <td class="num">2:00</td>
      <td>Core holds the pause, not arms · RPE 7</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

</details>

<!-- PHASE 3 -->
<details class="sec phase" id="phase3">
<summary><h2 class="p3">Phase 3 <span class="tag">Weeks 7–8+</span></h2></summary>
<p class="sub">Reintroduce rotation properly. Shallow drop knees on big holds, mirrored so the operated knee is directly compared against the healthy side. Heel hooks come absolutely last — they load the meniscus and hamstring attachment more than expected.</p>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Block A · Drop Knee Progression</h3><div class="freq">15:00–30:00 · both sessions</div></div>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Drill</th><th>Sets × Reps</th><th>Rest</th><th>Target / RPE</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Shallow drop knee holds — big foothold, knee rotates ≤45° down, hold the position statically.<span class="knee cau">Ease in over 2s · never snap into it</span></td>
      <td class="num">4 × 5 reps ×<br>5s hold (mirrored)</td>
      <td class="num">2:30</td>
      <td>Zero sharp/joint-line pain · RPE 6</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Drop knee ladder — link 4 moves using a shallow drop knee on alternating sides.</td>
      <td class="num">3 × 4 moves<br>(mirrored)</td>
      <td class="num">2:30</td>
      <td>Op-leg matches non-op smoothness · RPE 7</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Block B · Integration</h3><div class="freq">30:00–45:00 · both sessions</div></div>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Drill</th><th>Sets × Reps</th><th>Rest</th><th>Target / RPE</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Mixed-pattern circuit — 8 moves combining backstep, flag, high step, and one shallow drop knee.</td>
      <td class="num">4 × 8 moves<br>(mirrored)</td>
      <td class="num">3:00</td>
      <td>Fluid linking, no hesitation · RPE 7–8</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Heel hook introduction — large hold at hip height, load progressively to ~50% effort. <span class="note">Only if all drop-knee work is pain-free for 2 full sessions.</span><span class="knee cau">Wk 8+ · stop at any posterior knee pain</span></td>
      <td class="num">2 × 4 reps ×<br>5s (per leg)</td>
      <td class="num">2:00</td>
      <td>Sub-maximal only · RPE 5</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>

</details>

<!-- ENDURANCE -->
<details class="sec" id="endurance">
<summary><h2>Endurance <span class="tag" style="background:#EFE7FB;color:#7A4FD1">Session B · 15:00–40:00</span></h2></summary>
<p class="sub">Endurance work runs on Session B each week and progresses alongside the drill phases. It's knee-friendly by design — low intensity, big holds, static feet — so it starts in Week 1. On ARC blocks you should be able to hold a conversation; a deep forearm pump means the wall is too steep or the holds too small.</p>

